Tier 6 -- pseudo-cluster staged integration, shape A (reaper guest).

Three vnet jails as nodes on an internal bridge, real ZFS lineage, real ssh,
real CARP, and a fence driver whose "power off" stops the target jail. Named
stages, individually runnable: substrate, repl, interrupt, promote, quorum,
concurrency, failback, resurrection, hostile. See TESTING.md §7.

The substrate itself lives in tests/cluster/lib/cluster.subr and is asserted
by t_substrate.sh (stage 'substrate'): jails up, ssh mesh, delegated ZFS,
send/recv between jails, isolation, stop/start, teardown cleanliness,
up-down-up idempotence. Every later stage is entitled to assume all of that
and asserts none of it again.

Stage selection:

    SEANCE_STAGES=substrate,repl sh tests/run.sh   # a subset
    sh tests/run.sh                                # every stage

An unset or empty SEANCE_STAGES means all stages. A name that is not a known
stage is a contract error (exit 2), not a silent skip -- see
tests/cluster/lib/stage.subr, which each t_*.sh sources and calls
stage_begin <name> from before doing anything expensive.

These tests need root, ZFS, vnet jails and the reaper guest's own userland;
they do not run on the workstation.

Files named t_*.sh are tests; anything else here is ignored.
